Python Dependencies for Psychic-Tribble (i.e. interactive calendar app) 

Below is a comprehensive list of Python libraries (with corresponding GitHub repos) you’ll likely need for:

Core calendar functionality

Web/backend framework

Encryption and security

Shareable shortlink generation

User authentication & authorization

Email notifications

Utilities (env management, testing, formatting)

You can include these in your requirements.txt or install via pip at the top of your project.

1. Web Framework & API
Flask — lightweight WSGI framework • GitHub: https://github.com/pallets/flask • PyPI: Flask>=2.0

Flask-RESTful — build REST APIs on Flask • GitHub: https://github.com/flask-restful/flask-restful • PyPI: Flask-RESTful>=0.3.9

FastAPI — high-performance ASGI framework (optional) • GitHub: https://github.com/tiangolo/fastapi • PyPI: fastapi>=0.85

Uvicorn — ASGI server (for FastAPI) • GitHub: https://github.com/encode/uvicorn • PyPI: uvicorn>=0.18

2. Database & ORM
SQLAlchemy — core ORM and SQL toolkit • GitHub: https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy • PyPI: SQLAlchemy>=1.4

Flask-SQLAlchemy — SQLAlchemy integration for Flask • GitHub: https://github.com/pallets/flask-sqlalchemy • PyPI: Flask-SQLAlchemy>=2.5

Alembic — database migrations for SQLAlchemy • GitHub: https://github.com/sqlalchemy/alembic • PyPI: alembic>=1.7

psycopg2-binary — PostgreSQL driver (or choose mysqlclient) • PyPI: psycopg2-binary>=2.9

3. Calendar & Date-Time
icalendar — iCalendar RFC 5545 parsing/generation • GitHub: https://github.com/collective/icalendar • PyPI: icalendar>=4.0

ics.py — alternative iCal generator/parser • GitHub: https://github.com/C4ptAINCrunch/ics.py • PyPI: ics>=0.8

python-dateutil — recurrence rules, parsing • GitHub: https://github.com/dateutil/dateutil • PyPI: python-dateutil>=2.8

pytz — timezone database (or stdlib zoneinfo for Python 3.9+) • GitHub: https://github.com/stub42/pytz • PyPI: pytz>=2022.1

4. Authentication & Authorization
Flask-Login — session-based user management • GitHub: https://github.com/maxcountryman/flask-login • PyPI: Flask-Login>=0.6

Flask-JWT-Extended — JWT for RESTful auth • GitHub: https://github.com/vimalloc/flask-jwt-extended • PyPI: Flask-JWT-Extended>=4.4

PyJWT — encode/decode JSON Web Tokens • GitHub: https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt • PyPI: PyJWT>=2.4

passlib — secure password hashing (bcrypt, argon2) • GitHub: https://github.com/pallets/passlib • PyPI: passlib[bcrypt,argon2]>=1.7

5. Encryption & Security
cryptography — high-level cryptographic recipes • GitHub: https://github.com/pyca/cryptography • PyPI: cryptography>=38.0

itsdangerous — URL-safe data signing (tokens, links) • GitHub: https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous • PyPI: itsdangerous>=2.1

python-jose — JOSE (JWT/JWE/JWS) implementation (optional) • GitHub: https://github.com/mpdavis/python-jose • PyPI: python-jose>=3.3

6. Shortlink & Identifier Generation
hashids — generate short, unique, non-sequential IDs • GitHub: https://github.com/hashids/hashids-python • PyPI: hashids>=1.3

shortuuid — concise UUIDs • GitHub: https://github.com/skorokithakis/shortuuid • PyPI: shortuuid>=1.0

nanoid — URL-friendly unique string generator • GitHub: https://github.com/puyuan/py-nanoid • PyPI: nanoid>=0.7

7. Email & Notifications
Flask-Mail — SMTP integration for Flask • GitHub: https://github.com/mattupstate/flask-mail • PyPI: Flask-Mail>=0.9

aiosmtplib — async SMTP client (for FastAPI) • GitHub: https://github.com/cole/aiosmtplib • PyPI: aiosmtplib>=1.1

email-validator — validate email addresses • GitHub: https://github.com/JoshData/python-email-validator • PyPI: email-validator>=1.2

8. API & Data Validation
pydantic — data parsing & validation (FastAPI) • GitHub: https://github.com/samuelcolvin/pydantic • PyPI: pydantic>=1.10

marshmallow — schema-based (de)serialization • GitHub: https://github.com/marshmallow-code/marshmallow • PyPI: marshmallow>=3.14

9. Utilities & DevOps
python-dotenv — load .env configurations • GitHub: https://github.com/theskumar/python-dotenv • PyPI: python-dotenv>=0.20

requests / httpx — HTTP clients for external APIs • GitHub: https://github.com/psf/requests (PyPI: requests>=2.28) • GitHub: https://github.com/encode/httpx (PyPI: httpx>=0.24)

gunicorn — production WSGI server (for Flask) • GitHub: https://github.com/benoitc/gunicorn • PyPI: gunicorn>=20.1

pytest — testing framework • GitHub: https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest • PyPI: pytest>=7.1

black / isort — code formatting & import sorting • GitHub: https://github.com/psf/black (PyPI: black>=22.10) • GitHub: https://github.com/PyCQA/isort (PyPI: isort>=5.10)
